{
  "summary": "Fixes public key extraction for BIP-352 Silent Payments P2PKH inputs to prevent malleation attacks. Instead of executing scriptSig using EvalScript with a dummy signature checker, the extraction now iterates through opcodes to find a 33-byte data push whose hash matches the output script's pubkey hash.",
  "problem": "Third parties can malleate a P2PKH scriptSig with opcodes that fail real validation but pass the dummy signature checker used during silent payments key extraction. This leaves an attacker-controlled public key on top of the evaluation stack, causing silent payments wallets to scan using the wrong pubkey and miss incoming payments.",
  "evidence": [
    "Reported by Project Loupe, who discovered that malleated scriptSigs bypass the dummy signature checker in extraction.",
    "Included characterization test demonstrates that malleated spends remain consensus-valid while causing the existing dummy-checker evaluation to extract a wrong public key.",
    "Conforms to BIP-352: 'The receiver MUST parse the scriptSig for the public key, even if the scriptSig does not match the template specified.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Small patch (+62/-7) containing a regression/characterization test and the parsing fix; the diff text was omitted from the prompt.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Fixes BIP-352 Silent Payments pubkey extraction for P2PKH inputs by manually scanning scriptSig data pushes rather than running EvalScript with a dummy signature checker. Today, third parties can malleate a P2PKH scriptSig with conditional script opcodes that evaluate successfully under the dummy checker, tricking silent payments wallets into extracting the wrong public key and failing to detect incoming payments. The issue was discovered and reported by Project Loupe and is demonstrated by a new characterization test.",
